# Domain Value Object Conventions

- Class names must end with the suffix `ValueObject` (e.g. `MoneyValueObject`).
- Must override `GetHashCode()` and `Equals(object)`.
- Must implement `IEquatable<T>` where `T` is the value object type.
- Properties must not have public setters — value objects are immutable.

```csharp
// GOOD
namespace ClinicManagement.Domain.ValueObjects;

public class MoneyValueObject : ValueObject, IEquatable<MoneyValueObject>
{
    public decimal Amount { get; private set; }
    public string Currency { get; private set; }

    public bool Equals(MoneyValueObject? other) => /* ... */;
    public override bool Equals(object? obj) => /* ... */;
    public override int GetHashCode() => /* ... */;
}
```

```csharp
// BAD — public setter, missing suffix, no equality overrides
public class Money : ValueObject
{
    public decimal Amount { get; set; }
}
```
